      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nTucked away in a peaceful cul-de-sac just behind the heart of Shankill Village, this charming two-bedroom terraced home is a real hidden gem. Beautifully presented, completely renovated in recent years and ready to move straight into, the property combines a wonderful sense of warmth and character with an exceptionally convenient village location.\n\nThe house has undergone significant upgrading in recent years, including new PVC double- and triple-glazed windows throughout, a beautifully upgraded bathroom and a landscaped rear garden. Finished in a warm, neutral palette, the result is an inviting, turnkey home with a lovely sense of calm from the moment you step inside. It would be an excellent choice for first-time buyers, downsizers or anyone looking for an easily managed home in a settled and friendly neighbourhood.\nThe accommodation begins with an entrance porch leading into a wonderfully bright and welcoming living room. The staircase is positioned here, while the neutral décor and excellent natural light create a comfortable and homely space. To the rear lies the kitchen and dining area, another particularly bright room thanks to a large bay window and glazed door which allow natural light to flood the space. There is ample kitchen storage and a lovely outlook over the rear garden, making this a very pleasant room for both everyday living and entertaining. The kitchen opens directly onto the private, south-west-facing landscaped garden. Designed with low maintenance in mind and benefiting from excellent afternoon and evening sunshine, it is a wonderful extension of the living accommodation during the warmer months. Importantly, the garden is not overlooked to the rear, providing a welcome sense of privacy that is unusual for such a central village location.\n\nUpstairs are two generous double bedrooms, both complemented by large fitted wardrobes providing excellent storage. The bathroom has also been recently renovated to a particularly high standard and is finished with full tiling, stylish brushed-brass fittings, an upgraded WC and wash-hand basin, and a contemporary rainfall shower.\n\nOne of the property's greatest attractions, however, is its location. Tucked just behind Brady's Pub and moments from the centre of Shankill Village, the house enjoys all the convenience of village life while remaining remarkably peaceful and secluded. Shankill is a long-established and highly sought-after south Dublin neighbourhood, with an excellent selection of local shops, cafés, services and amenities close at hand.\n\nThe area is particularly well served for families, with a choice of excellent schools nearby, while Shankill Beach and the area's parks and green spaces provide fantastic opportunities for walking, recreation and enjoying the outdoors. Transport connections are another major advantage, with local bus services and Shankill DART station providing convenient access to the city centre and along the coast. The Luas at Brides Glen is also within easy reach, while motorists have excellent access to the N11 and M50, making commuting throughout Dublin and beyond particularly convenient.\n\nBeautifully renovated, wonderfully bright and genuinely turnkey, this is a home with an abundance of charm. Its peaceful cul-de-sac setting, private sunny garden, excellent neighbours and superb position in the heart of Shankill combine to create a property that is not only extremely convenient, but somewhere that would be very easy to call home.\n\nKey Features\n\n• Beautifully presented two-bedroom terraced home in turnkey condition\n• Completely renovated and upgraded in recent years\n• New PVC double- and triple-glazed windows throughout\n• Stylish, recently renovated fully tiled bathroom with brushed-brass fittings and rainfall shower\n• Bright kitchen/dining room with large bay window and excellent garden outlook\n• Private, landscaped south-west-facing rear garden, enjoying afternoon and evening sunshine\n• Rear garden is not overlooked, offering an excellent degree of privacy\n• Peaceful cul-de-sac setting in the heart of Shankill Village, just behind Brady's Pub\n• Superb location close to excellent schools, Shankill Beach, parks, shops, cafés and village amenities\n• Excellent transport links including Shankill DART station, local bus routes, Luas at Brides Glen, N11 and M50"
      },
      {
